    <!-- faq-section sTARTS -->

    <section class="faq-section py-4 py-lg-5 ">
        <div class="custom-container">

            <div class="outlined-green rounded-pill overflow-hidden d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center"
                data-aos="fade-right" data-aos-delay="0">
                <div class="text rounded-pill  h-100 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center">
                    FAQs
                </div>
            </div>
            <h2 class="heading-medium text-start aos-init aos-animate d-block d-lg-none" data-aos="fade-right"
                data-aos-delay="400">
                Frequently Asked Questions
            </h2>

            <!-- <h2 class="heading-medium text-start" data-aos="fade-right" data-aos-delay="400">
                    Frequently Asked Questions
                </h2> -->

            <div class="row g-4">
                <div class="col-lg-7" data-aos="fade-right" data-aos-delay="400" data-aos-duration="1000">

                    <div class="accordion mb-4 mb-lg-0" id="accordionExample2">

                        <!-- FAQ 1 -->
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <div class="accordion-header">
                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                    data-bs-target="#collapseaOne" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseaOne">
                                    <svg class="inline-flex" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="21" height="20"
                                        viewBox="0 0 21 20" fill="none">
                                        <path
                                            d="M4.80477 19.981C4.44165 19.981 4.05942 19.8673 3.75363 19.6398C3.16118 19.2038 2.91273 18.4265 3.14207 17.7251L4.78566 12.4929L0.619345 9.13744C0.0651115 8.66351 -0.145115 7.90521 0.103335 7.22275C0.351785 6.54028 1.02069 6.08531 1.74693 6.08531H7.00259L8.85641 1.13744C9.10486 0.454977 9.77376 0 10.5 0C11.2262 0 11.8951 0.454977 12.1436 1.13744L13.9974 6.08531H19.2531C19.9793 6.08531 20.6482 6.54028 20.8967 7.22275C21.1451 7.90521 20.9349 8.68246 20.3807 9.1564L16.2335 12.5118L17.9535 17.6872C18.1828 18.3886 17.9535 19.1659 17.361 19.6019C16.7686 20.0569 15.9659 20.0758 15.3352 19.6777L10.5191 16.5687L5.77946 19.7156C5.49278 19.9052 5.14878 20 4.80477 20V19.981Z"
                                            fill="#FAAD1A" />
                                    </svg>
                                    <span class="ms-2 inline-flex">Do I need prior programming experience to
                                        join?</span>
                                </button>
                            </div>
                            <div id="collapseaOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                data-bs-parent="#accordionExample2">
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    No prior programming experience is required. Our curriculum is designed to take you
                                    from zero to job-ready — starting with the fundamentals of embedded C and building
                                    up through RTOS, Linux, and IoT protocols. As long as you're motivated and willing
                                    to get your hands on real hardware, you're ready to begin.
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- FAQ 2 -->
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <div class="accordion-header">
                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                    data-bs-target="#collapseaTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseaTwo">
                                    <svg class="inline-flex" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="21" height="20"
                                        viewBox="0 0 21 20" fill="none">
                                        <path
                                            d="M4.80477 19.981C4.44165 19.981 4.05942 19.8673 3.75363 19.6398C3.16118 19.2038 2.91273 18.4265 3.14207 17.7251L4.78566 12.4929L0.619345 9.13744C0.0651115 8.66351 -0.145115 7.90521 0.103335 7.22275C0.351785 6.54028 1.02069 6.08531 1.74693 6.08531H7.00259L8.85641 1.13744C9.10486 0.454977 9.77376 0 10.5 0C11.2262 0 11.8951 0.454977 12.1436 1.13744L13.9974 6.08531H19.2531C19.9793 6.08531 20.6482 6.54028 20.8967 7.22275C21.1451 7.90521 20.9349 8.68246 20.3807 9.1564L16.2335 12.5118L17.9535 17.6872C18.1828 18.3886 17.9535 19.1659 17.361 19.6019C16.7686 20.0569 15.9659 20.0758 15.3352 19.6777L10.5191 16.5687L5.77946 19.7156C5.49278 19.9052 5.14878 20 4.80477 20V19.981Z"
                                            fill="#FAAD1A" />
                                    </svg>
                                    <span class="ms-2 inline-flex">What kind of real devices will I work with?</span>
                                </button>
                            </div>
                            <div id="collapseaTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                data-bs-parent="#accordionExample2">
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    You'll get hands-on with industry-standard hardware including microcontrollers (ARM
                                    Cortex-M series), Raspberry Pi for Embedded Linux, and dedicated IoT development
                                    boards. Projects involve real sensors, actuators, wireless modules (MQTT/BLE/Wi-Fi),
                                    and Edge AI inference hardware — not simulators, not emulators, real devices.
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- FAQ 3 -->
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <div class="accordion-header">
                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                    data-bs-target="#collapseaThree" aria-expanded="false"
                                    aria-controls="collapseaThree">
                                    <svg class="inline-flex" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="21" height="20"
                                        viewBox="0 0 21 20" fill="none">
                                        <path
                                            d="M4.80477 19.981C4.44165 19.981 4.05942 19.8673 3.75363 19.6398C3.16118 19.2038 2.91273 18.4265 3.14207 17.7251L4.78566 12.4929L0.619345 9.13744C0.0651115 8.66351 -0.145115 7.90521 0.103335 7.22275C0.351785 6.54028 1.02069 6.08531 1.74693 6.08531H7.00259L8.85641 1.13744C9.10486 0.454977 9.77376 0 10.5 0C11.2262 0 11.8951 0.454977 12.1436 1.13744L13.9974 6.08531H19.2531C19.9793 6.08531 20.6482 6.54028 20.8967 7.22275C21.1451 7.90521 20.9349 8.68246 20.3807 9.1564L16.2335 12.5118L17.9535 17.6872C18.1828 18.3886 17.9535 19.1659 17.361 19.6019C16.7686 20.0569 15.9659 20.0758 15.3352 19.6777L10.5191 16.5687L5.77946 19.7156C5.49278 19.9052 5.14878 20 4.80477 20V19.981Z"
                                            fill="#FAAD1A" />
                                    </svg>
                                    <span class="ms-2 inline-flex">Is this program online, offline, or hybrid?</span>
                                </button>
                            </div>
                            <div id="collapseaThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                data-bs-parent="#accordionExample2">
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    We offer a hybrid model — live online sessions with instructors, supplemented by
                                    in-person lab days for hardware projects. If you're remote, a hardware kit is
                                    shipped to you so you can build on real devices from wherever you are. You'll never
                                    be stuck watching someone else code on a projector.
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- FAQ 4 -->
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <div class="accordion-header">
                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                    data-bs-target="#collapsea4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapsea4">
                                    <svg class="inline-flex" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="21" height="20"
                                        viewBox="0 0 21 20" fill="none">
                                        <path
                                            d="M4.80477 19.981C4.44165 19.981 4.05942 19.8673 3.75363 19.6398C3.16118 19.2038 2.91273 18.4265 3.14207 17.7251L4.78566 12.4929L0.619345 9.13744C0.0651115 8.66351 -0.145115 7.90521 0.103335 7.22275C0.351785 6.54028 1.02069 6.08531 1.74693 6.08531H7.00259L8.85641 1.13744C9.10486 0.454977 9.77376 0 10.5 0C11.2262 0 11.8951 0.454977 12.1436 1.13744L13.9974 6.08531H19.2531C19.9793 6.08531 20.6482 6.54028 20.8967 7.22275C21.1451 7.90521 20.9349 8.68246 20.3807 9.1564L16.2335 12.5118L17.9535 17.6872C18.1828 18.3886 17.9535 19.1659 17.361 19.6019C16.7686 20.0569 15.9659 20.0758 15.3352 19.6777L10.5191 16.5687L5.77946 19.7156C5.49278 19.9052 5.14878 20 4.80477 20V19.981Z"
                                            fill="#FAAD1A" />
                                    </svg>
                                    <span class="ms-2 inline-flex">Does the program cover AI and TinyML or just embedded
                                        basics?</span>
                                </button>
                            </div>
                            <div id="collapsea4" class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                                data-bs-parent="#accordionExample2">
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    Both — and everything in between. The curriculum spans the full stack: Embedded C →
                                    RTOS → Embedded Linux → IoT Protocols → Edge AI → TinyML → Generative AI in IoT. By
                                    the end, you'll be deploying ML models on microcontrollers and building AI-driven
                                    IoT systems, not just blinking LEDs.
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- FAQ 5 -->
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <div class="accordion-header">
                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                    data-bs-target="#collapsea5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapsea5">
